        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity 276",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity 276\n\nsanity test_276 races OST mount against obd_statfs by looping\nOST stop/start cycles, roughly 8 seconds each, for 120 seconds\n(LU-20076), plus 600 more with SLOW=yes.  It runs about 17000\ntimes per 30 days at a mean of 158 seconds.\n\nThe race is probabilistic, so what catches a regression is the\ntotal number of cycles across all sessions, not the length of\nany one run.  Cap the loop at 30 seconds, about 4 cycles, in\nnormal runs.  That is still about 70000 cycles a month in CI\naggregate.  This partly walks back the LU-20076 choice of 120\nseconds per run, on the same argument.  SLOW=yes runs keep the\n720 second loop.\n\nOn a test VM, ONLY=276 took 126s, 125s and 125s before, and\n106s (first run after redeploy), 35s, 36s, 35s, 35s and 35s\nafter.  Expected CI saving is about 90s per run x 17274 runs\nper 30 days, about 430 hours.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=276\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ic6df0d6e6c28755a4cb77ddf7ef2d0aaca2b6ac4\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70184\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Deiter <adeiter@ddn.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
